nswer/id #uuid "62d09325-3296-583d-8345-a494c90bbefa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{s-4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312761} {:answer/id #uuid "f164c249-51ae-54ce-a419-588febef9cc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{4s-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313909}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f164c249-51ae-54ce-a419-588febef9cc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{4s-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313909} :answer-field/id #uuid "eae43bfc-8ecf-5213-a5ac-2da4bee05982" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314655}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4c2a792f-5d39-57d4-96e7-654fb5bc6512" :question/math-academy-id "q-340731" :question/problem "Complete the arguments in the reasoning below to find the Laplace transform of $f(t)={e}^{t/4}.$First, we apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\nL{f(t)}=F(s)={{field-1}}\n$$\n\nWe now examine the convergence of $F(s)$ for different values of $s:$\n\n$\\,$ For {{field-2}}\nthe integral is convergent.\n\n$\\,$ For {{field-3}}\nthe integral is divergent.\n\nEvaluating our integral in the convergent case, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{(1/4-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t={{field-4}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $L{{e}^{t/4}}=\\frac{4}{4s-1},$ \ndefined for\n{{field-5}}." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(t)$ defined on $[0,\\infty ),$ the Laplace transform of $f,$ denoted $L{f(t)}$ or $F(s),$ is a function of the variable $s$ defined as\n\n$$\nF(s)=L{f(t)}={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nprovided that this integral exists and is finite. \n\nFor the function $f(t)={e}^{t/4},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\cdot {e}^{t/4}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st+t/4}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{(1/4-s)t}\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{(1/4-s)t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}{e}^{(1/4-s)t}\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo evaluate the last integral, we must consider whether $s\\ne \\frac{1}{4}$ or $s=\\frac{1}{4}.$\n\n- If $s\\ne \\frac{1}{4},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}{e}^{(1/4-s)t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{1}{1/4-s}{e}^{(1/4-s)t})|}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1/4-s}({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{(1/4-s)a}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s-1/4}(1-{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{(1/4-s)a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s-1/4}-\\frac{1}{s-1/4}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{(1/4-s)a}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's evaluate the limit. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{(1/4-s)a}={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & s>\\frac{1}{4}, \\\\ \\infty ,\\, & s<\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $s=\\frac{1}{4},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(\\frac{1}{4}) & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}{e}^{(1/4-1/4)t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}{e}^{0t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }t\\,{|}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(a-0) \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }a \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- For $s>\\frac{1}{4}$ the integral is convergent.\n\n- For $s\\le \\frac{1}{4}$ the integral is divergent.\n\nEvaluating for $s>\\frac{1}{4},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & =\\frac{1}{s-1/4}-\\frac{1}{s-1/4}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{(1/4-s)a} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s-1/4}-\\frac{1}{s-1/4}\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s-1/4} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{4s-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the Laplace transform of $f(t)={e}^{t/4}$ is $F(s)=\\frac{4}{4s-1},$ defined for $s>\\frac{1}{4}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315005 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "044ca0d4-aaba-5302-985d-4a3914497689" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311994} {:answer/id #uuid "3e7cc5f4-57f4-5585-a618-ea327dba24d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\le \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312480} {:answer/id #uuid "df9cd9d1-0fd8-5400-891b-0d6ec4ad99aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313732}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "044ca0d4-aaba-5302-985d-4a3914497689" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311994} :answer-field/id #uuid "2db18bec-06a0-594e-b7f1-4a2e90ccd8a8" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314133} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62037aa0-fad6-5dd5-ab7d-d8c263d3d831" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\le \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312757} {:answer/id #uuid "91b8f5d9-b490-538d-afc1-6a61a3465c85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313140}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91b8f5d9-b490-538d-afc1-6a61a3465c85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313140} :answer-field/id #uuid "423238ea-22d4-5e02-839f-7b32d68d897d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/