:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313651}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4bf5cf5-aad6-5bed-8091-42b190f12f2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313651} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1db4855-6479-5ff6-8518-b6f5bdd97377" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314632}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3bc082e0-e258-5a86-b2f6-5e93b65fda0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-340899" :question/problem "Suppose we wish to calculate the Laplace transform \n\n$$\nL{t\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t}.\n$$\n\n \nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below. You may make use of the following result:\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}},\\,s>0.\n$$\n\nLet $f(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t$ and $L{f(t)}=F(s).$ By the smoothness property of Laplace transforms,\n\n$$\nL{tf(t)}={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe Laplace transform of $f(t)$ is\n\n$$\nF(s)=L{f(t)}={{field-2}},\\,s>0.\n$$\n\nWe have that\n\n$$\n{F}^{′}(s)={{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nL{t\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t}={{field-4}},\\,s>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If a function $f(t)$ is piecewise continuous on $[0,\\infty )$ and has exponential order $a,$ then its Laplace transform\n\n$$\nF(s)=L{f(t)}\n$$\n\nexists for every real $s>a,$ and $F$ is infinitely differentiable in this region of convergence. Moreover, for each integer $n\\ge 0$ and every such $s,$ we have\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{n}f(t)}=(-1)^{n}{F}^{(n)}(s).\n$$\n\nIn particular, for $n=1,$ we have\n\n$$\nL{tf(t)}=-{F}^{′}(s).\n$$\n\nWe have that $f(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t.$ Using the given result with $\\omega =4,$ the Laplace transform of $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nF(s)=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+16},\\,s>0.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating with respect to $s,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+16}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(s({s}^{2}+16)^{-1}) \\\\  & =({s}^{2}+16)^{-1}+s(-({s}^{2}+16)^{-2}\\cdot 2s) \\\\  & =\\frac{{s}^{2}+16}{({s}^{2}+16)^{2}}-\\frac{2{s}^{2}}{({s}^{2}+16)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{16-{s}^{2}}{({s}^{2}+16)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by the smoothness property,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{t\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t}=-{F}^{′}(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}-16}{({s}^{2}+16)^{2}},\\,s>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315035 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0393ece1-72d0-5a26-86d5-ccbeeaf37ae2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311992} {:answer/id #uuid "597f53c7-4437-514a-af3b-d52acd9b2c49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312692} {:answer/id #uuid "8fa014c5-9b63-5c2d-9789-24fc078e3a74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313121} {:answer/id #uuid "94ca3393-2d0c-5d35-8160-e4662eb26e90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313168}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "597f53c7-4437-514a-af3b-d52acd9b2c49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312692} :answer-field/id #uuid "38fae9d9-cbd3-5455-8427-b745a060a7d6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314166} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "664a4c96-a01f-59cb-967b-ffb4901c3599" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s}+\\frac{2}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312781} {:answer/id #uuid "7f5c2bf1-f5e6-5b17-9d72-cc0c282c3bb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s}-\\frac{2}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312999} {:answer/id #uuid "8bd2bb9a-325d-5590-893b-654f04aa3611" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{e}^{-4s}}{s}+\\frac{1}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313092} {:answer/id #uuid "b056a71c-b807-5605-908f-a02ed7bf64a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{s}-\\frac{2{e}^{-4s}}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313347} {:answer/id #uuid "c0cc3710-19e9-51a7-83aa-4c898958b227" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{e}^{-4s}}{s}-\\frac{1}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313485}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0cc3710-19e9-51a7-83aa-4c898958b227" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{e}^{-4s}}{s}-\\frac{1}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313485} :answer-field/id #uuid "a284234b-2957-5483-83fc-1e261cf48e0f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314449}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1b3b95d4-60c8-526c-96a6-a82f623ad04d" :question/math-academy-id "q-340932" :question/problem "Use the definition of Laplace transforms to calculate $F(s)=L{f(t)},$ where $f(t)$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(t)={\\begin{aligned}-1,\\, & x\\le 4 \\\\ 1\\, & x>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$\\,F(s)=L{f(t)}=$ {{field-1}},\nvalid for {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "We apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for the piecewise function \n\n$$\nf(t)={\\begin{aligned}-1,\\, & x\\le 4 \\\\ 1\\, & x>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}(-1)\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }1\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{0}^{4}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the improper integral diverges if $s\\le 0.$\n\nFor $s>0,$ we calculate our Laplace transform as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & =-{\\int }_{0}^{4}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s}{[{e}^{-st}]}_{0}^{4}+{\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s}-\\frac{1}{s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{4}^{a}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s}-\\frac{1}{s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(-\\frac{{e}^{-st}}{s})|}_{4}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s}-\\frac{1}{s}-\\frac{1}{s}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }({e}^{-sa}-{e}^{-4s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s}-\\frac{1}{s}-\\frac{1}{s}(0-{e}^{-4s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s}-\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{e}^{-4s}}{s}-\\frac{1}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nvalid for $s>0.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315036 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8aacf8a-923a-5706-a78c-108e65099a32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313826}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8aacf8a-923a-5706-a78c-108e65099a32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313826} :answer-field/id #uuid "55ac9af9-f5be-5aac-9b98-a73bb56de950" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314252} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f398213-9b43-5009-a712-5e39a192aab2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312352}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f398213-9b43-5009-a712-5e39a192aab2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312352} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1e679c8-0512-5ea7-a995-5f08819c8352" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314554}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6db0058b-56f3-5a30-bae9-0cf86c420390" :question/math-academy-id "q-340945" :question/problem "Find the equation of the normal line to the curve $y=\\frac{8}{{x}^{2}}$ at the point $(2,2).$\n\n$x\\,-$\n{{field-1}}$\\cdot \\,y\\,=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=\\frac{8}{{x}^{2}}.$ First, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{8}{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8{x}^{-2}) \\\\  & =-16{x}^{-3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{16}{{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the slope of the tangent at the point $(2,2):$\n\n$$\nm={f}^{′}(2)=-\\frac{16}{(2)^{3}}=-\\frac{16}{8}=-2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the normal line is\n\n$$\n{m}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{-2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(2) & =\\frac{1}{2}(x-2) \\\\ 2y-4 & =x-2 \\\\ x-2\\cdot y & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315039 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "392b0b79-8325-51e9-80af-b0e2db96f3cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312438}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "392b0b79-8325-51e9-80af-b0e2db96f3cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312438} :answer-field/id #uuid "3aba0483-9c05-5996-9c78-df0105e89050" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314172}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f44134b3-2bb1-57f7-a413-41c3c3c73af6" :question/math-academy-id "q-341011" :question/problem "The values of functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=0$ are given in the table below. \n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ | ${g}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $4$ | $-1$ | $2$ |\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})$ at $x=0.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=0}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})=\\frac{{f}^{′}(x)g(x)-f(x){g}^{′}(x)}{(g(x))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=0$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=0} & =\\frac{{f}^{′}(0)g(0)-f(0){g}^{′}(0)}{(g(0))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)(4)-(\\frac{1}{2})(2)}{{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4-1}{16} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315040 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb50bd7f-39cc-56cb-aa5b-7218d902f777" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313435}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb50bd7f-39cc-56cb-aa5b-7218d902f777" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313435} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0182abb-5f03-5f80-a3dd-0dc6384897c9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314543}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "65226573-de55-55b8-bdde-6256c33bf52d" :question/math-academy-id "q-341013" :question/problem "For the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x),$ you are given the following data:\n\n$$\nf(4)=2,\\,{f}^{′}(4)=\\sqrt{2},\\,g(4)=\\sqrt{2},\\,{g}^{′}(4)=-1\n$$\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})$ at $x=4.$\n\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=4}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})=\\frac{{f}^{′}(x)g(x)-f(x){g}^{′}(x)}{(g(x))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=4,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=4} & =\\frac{{f}^{′}(4)g(4)-f(4){g}^{′}(4)}{(g(4))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}-2\\cdot (-1)}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2+2}{2} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315045 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07634376-05f7-5c3f-a0aa-27add524b643" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{{s}^{2}+49}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312024} {:answer/id #uuid "17ef972b-f314-526b-81aa-e2ce319165ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+49}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312145} {:answer/id #uuid "3d3a0c6b-7abe-5d48-aea0-64a847e3d2a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{{s}^{2}-49}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312470} {:answer/id #uuid "4de4061e-d72d-5f53-83b8-8dc072e09abf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-49}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312609}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4de4061e-d72d-5f53-83b8-8dc072e09abf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-49}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312609} :answer-field/id #uuid "0aaecc08-c488-5535-bed2-98e522543499" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314042} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b77274b-8e09-5a1d-b705-a0e7719f885b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{{s}^{2}+49}{({s}^{2}-49)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312961} {:answer/id #uuid "ac063add-bea7-5ba0-b649-21d4458ad2f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7{s}^{2}}{({s}^{2}-49)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313322} {:answer/id #uuid "c1f61ad3-eb33-5aa8-927c-d2f7509ce42c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7{s}^{2}}{({s}^{2}-49)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313495} {:answer/id #uuid "fe5ff3e8-7f8c-52ae-8226-82d4f946a9f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{s}^{2}+49}{({s}^{2}-49)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314006}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe5ff3e8-7f8c-52ae-8226-82d4f946a9f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{s}^{2}+49}{({s}^{2}-49)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314006} :answer-field/id #uuid "207371ec-451d-5fcc-a161-3d364f3bc157" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314096} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06d56ae4-3645-5032-b8c8-47b6ae2c13eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s{F}^{′}(s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312021} {:answer/id #uuid "2e8fa295-1370-5bab-a160-708121a10dee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{F}^{′}(s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312341} {:answer/id #uuid "396c3982-db2f-5948-a96e-54c0e12b4705" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-s{F}^{′}(s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312441} {:answer/id #uuid "ab5ee628-6197-5596-bd0c-cb3cf17c4546" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-F(s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313318} {:answer/id #uuid "d16b16f9-269e-56d8-847c-9242e7fc0377" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{F}^{′}(s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313612}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d16b16f9-269e-56d8-847c-9242e7fc0377" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{F}^{′}(s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313612} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ec379e4-6326-5470-b34e-2a9f7a36b67f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314394} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32ab0471-9ab5-5d94-9472-9c9745ccd041" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7{s}^{2}}{({s}^{2}-49)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312385} {:answer/id #uuid "68430b40-6d63-5c5b-bafe-6b99044058d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{s}^{2}+49}{({s}^{2}-49)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312793} {:answer/id #uuid "d112e8a6-b00c-5763-974e-6a78131a0a11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{{s}^{2}+49}{({s}^{2}-49)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313608} {:answer/id #uuid "d1ddf551-1124-5b15-bae0-588313713cea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7{s}^{2}}{({s}^{2}-49)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313614}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d112e8a6-b00c-5763-974e-6a78131a0a11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{{s}^{2}+49}{({s}^{2}-49)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313608} :answer-field/id #uuid "bbe32a19-a038-5a1c-9adb-5fab337cee14" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314525}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ed378e80-6795-5ad0-8973-5105f9a33be1" :question/math-academy-id "q-341050" :question/problem "Suppose we wish to calculate the Laplace transform \n\n$$\nL{t\\operatorname{cosh}⁡7t}.\n$$\n\n \nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below. You may make use of the following result:\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡\\omega t}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-{\\omega }^{2}},\\,s>\\omega .\n$$\n\nLet $f(t)=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡7t$ and $L{f(t)}=F(s).$ By the smoothness property of Laplace transforms,\n\n$$\nL{tf(t)}={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe Laplace transform of $f(t)$ is\n\n$$\nF(s)=L{f(t)}={{field-2}},\\,s>7.\n$$\n\nWe have that\n\n$$\n{F}^{′}(s)={{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nL{t\\operatorname{cosh}⁡7t}={{field-4}},\\,s>7.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If a function $f(t)$ is piecewise continuous on $[0,\\infty )$ and has exponential order $a,$ then its Laplace transform\n\n$$\nF(s)=L{f(t)}\n$$\n\nexists for every real $s>a,$ and $F$ is infinitely differentiable in this region of convergence. Moreover, for each integer $n\\ge 0$ and every such $s,$ we have\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{n}f(t)}=(-1)^{n}{F}^{(n)}(s).\n$$\n\nIn particular, for $n=1,$ we have\n\n$$\nL{tf(t)}=-{F}^{′}(s).\n$$\n\nWe have that $f(t)=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡7t.$ Using the given result with $\\omega =7,$ the Laplace transform of $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nF(s)=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-49},\\,s>7.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating with respect to $s,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-49}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(s({s}^{2}-49)^{-1}) \\\\  & =({s}^{2}-49)^{-1}+s(-({s}^{2}-49)^{-2}\\cdot 2s) \\\\  & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-49}{({s}^{2}-49)^{2}}-\\frac{2{s}^{2}}{({s}^{2}-49)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-49-{s}^{2}}{({s}^{2}-49)^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{s}^{2}+49}{({s}^{2}-49)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by the smoothness property,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{t\\operatorname{cosh}⁡7t}=-{F}^{′}(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}+49}{({s}^{2}-49)^{2}},\\,s>7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315048 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8ee806f-7719-5298-ac62-41e17b9b6edb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313414}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8ee806f-7719-5298-ac62-41e17b9b6edb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313414} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3d1446c-0422-5804-ab35-51c287ebd71b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314497}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3d8da40e-cfdf-5c60-a36a-cdb26f7bb8fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-341104" :question/problem "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the curve $y=2x+arccotx$ at $x=0.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $arccot$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccot\\,x)=-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x+arccotx) \\\\  & =2+(-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =2-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at $x=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={y}^{′}(0) & =2-\\frac{1}{1+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =2-1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315049 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "736358be-b15d-5572-9a7d-e2c1b162c5fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312889} {:answer/id #uuid "b6d51f45-9ac3-50b7-8e7e-a99791f5df84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313397} {:answer/id #uuid "bcb7f8c7-f0ee-5b82-8e68-9bf292adfc5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313448} {:answer/id #uuid "ca011ffd-4317-5cd0-a523-b8d946003250" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313551} {:answer/id #uuid "cd2f2e3a-830c-5c61-97de-1eeed7ae62c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313580} {:answer/id #uuid "fd385b6a-f413-51e4-8c07-5e53e44b0516" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313995}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "736358be-b15d-5572-9a7d-e2c1b162c5fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312889} :answer-field/id #uuid "c97fbae0-d928-5e16-8119-2ca0e620f0dc" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314569} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a9aeaa1-b187-5b93-9a34-d4e755e38dd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312170} {:answer/id #uuid "3de705a6-c93c-5847-aef8-686296cd036d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312475} {:answer/id #uuid "65422943-54ca-5806-b182-99db46b4b27f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312773} {:answer/id #uuid "67ae037d-6d7f-5de0-9976-57829f55953f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2s}{{s}^{2}-4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312789} {:answer/id #uuid "c98c24e1-c972-56c4-ba20-92ddfb1aa44c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}-4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313546}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3de705a6-c93c-5847-aef8-686296cd036d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312475} :answer-field/id #uuid "ddaee052-1803-54cd-a0f9-ce0838d40348" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314625}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f2c45534-de22-5957-94a0-9fb0be556b3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-341107" :question/problem "Use the Laplace transform of $f(t)={e}^{kt}$ to find the Laplace transform of $\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t).$$\\,L{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)}=$ {{field-1}},\ndefined for {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The linearity property of the Laplace transform states that for functions $f(t)$ and $g(t),$ we have\n\n$$\nL{\\alpha f(t)+\\beta g(t)}=\\alpha \\cdot L{f(t)}+\\beta \\cdot L{g(t)},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants.\n\nFirst, recall that, by definition\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)=\\frac{{e}^{2t}+{e}^{-2t}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTaking the Laplace transform and applying the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)} & =L{\\frac{{e}^{2t}+{e}^{-2t}}{2}} \\\\  & =L{\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{2}+\\frac{{e}^{-2t}}{2}} \\\\  & =L{\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{2}}+L{\\frac{{e}^{-2t}}{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{2t}}+\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{-2t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we recall that \n\n$$\nL{{e}^{kt}}=\\frac{1}{s-k},\\,s>k.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{2t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-2},\\,s>2 \\\\ L{{e}^{-2t}} & =\\frac{1}{s+2},\\,s>-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)} & =\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{2t}}+\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{-2t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s-2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{s-2}+\\frac{1}{s+2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{(s+2)+(s-2)}{(s-2)(s+2)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{2s}{{s}^{2}-4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $L{{e}^{2t}}$ is defined for $s\\in (2,\\infty )$ and $L{{e}^{-2t}}$ is defined for $s\\in (-2,\\infty ),$ we have that $L{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)}$ is defined for\n\n$$\n(2,\\infty )\\cap (-2,\\infty )=(2,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nthat is, $s>2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315050 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8edf9692-6828-531e-a524-456c401eb354" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313116} {:answer/id #uuid "b3f609bf-30c3-5195-9625-8bf23dbeb98e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4s}{{s}^{2}-16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313373} {:answer/id #uuid "c61fae7a-d115-5d60-aace-221720a5ea31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}-16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313528} {:answer/id #uuid "cf692c6b-eaf1-58f2-b0cd-fa16ba85d66e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313596} {:answer/id #uuid "e428bf77-631f-59d6-9120-f9ce05a41509" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313775}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf692c6b-eaf1-58f2-b0cd-fa16ba85d66e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313596} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0a66528-692d-5c78-823d-ade5dfdc33d5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314441} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f73f9f2-9a84-5ff9-bd27-5d1e9f589c25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312738} {:answer/id #uuid "7e6fd869-adbf-5e44-889c-f05617df5aeb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312991} {:answer/id #uuid "830640f3-0e0d-5579-a43f-b99d0dd807e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313029} {:answer/id #uuid "a27becd5-454a-566a-b4cc-a33c60c4d7e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge -4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313253} {:answer/id #uuid "a84b7be1-8f52-5f7a-a33f-707976201760" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313295} {:answer/id #uuid "ec1ce046-09b5-5e82-bc8c-ef125afe175a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313861}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e6fd869-adbf-5e44-889c-f05617df5aeb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312991} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6cd3403-b426-5f6c-ad5f-b0f06b27b7e2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314604}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "25fdc2a1-548f-5db7-a267-7ea03400402a" :question/math-academy-id "q-341109" :question/problem "Use the Laplace transform of $f(t)={e}^{kt}$ to find the Laplace transform of $\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t).$$\\,L{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)}=$ {{field-1}},\ndefined for {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The linearity property of the Laplace transform states that for functions $f(t)$ and $g(t),$ we have\n\n$$\nL{\\alpha f(t)+\\beta g(t)}=\\alpha \\cdot L{f(t)}+\\beta \\cdot L{g(t)},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants.\n\nFirst, recall that, by definition\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)=\\frac{{e}^{4t}+{e}^{-4t}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTaking the Laplace transform and applying the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)} & =L{\\frac{{e}^{4t}+{e}^{-4t}}{2}} \\\\  & =L{\\frac{{e}^{4t}}{2}+\\frac{{e}^{-4t}}{2}} \\\\  & =L{\\frac{{e}^{4t}}{2}}+L{\\frac{{e}^{-4t}}{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{4t}}+\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{-4t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we recall that \n\n$$\nL{{e}^{kt}}=\\frac{1}{s-k},\\,s>k.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{4t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-4},\\,s>4 \\\\ L{{e}^{-4t}} & =\\frac{1}{s+4},\\,s>-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)} & =\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{4t}}+\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{-4t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s-4}+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{s-4}+\\frac{1}{s+4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{(s+4)+(s-4)}{(s-4)(s+4)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{2s}{{s}^{2}-16}) \\\\  & =\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $L{{e}^{4t}}$ is defined for $s\\in (4,\\infty )$ and $L{{e}^{-4t}}$ is defined for $s\\in (-4,\\infty ),$ we have that $L{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)}$ is defined for\n\n$$\n(4,\\infty )\\cap (-4,\\infty )=(4,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nthat is, $s>4.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315053 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c768e14f-5c12-58a7-a2f6-c76213bf259b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12s}{{s}^{2}+144}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313533} {:answer/id #uuid "da0c792d-19bb-5761-a855-22981a61e7f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+144}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313689} {:answer/id #uuid "ebfaea01-08ad-5f2d-b3c4-35c19ceb7293" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-144}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313860} {:answer/id #uuid "faf65d46-a67b-54cf-9a43-1928028845c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{{s}^{2}+144}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313979} {:answer/id #uuid "ff66dd4e-ce1c-53e8-b03e-2493d92b1a66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{{s}^{2}-144}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314013}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "faf65d46-a67b-54cf-9a43-1928028845c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{{s}^{2}+144}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313979} :answer-field/id #uuid "25c56102-996d-591d-9850-f3779725766d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314109} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b1e4833-125b-5275-9ddb-3e5a0c5c0ef5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312308} {:answer/id #uuid "4344e22b-2cf4-5526-888c-708789e7646f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312512} {:answer/id #uuid "4489bac6-a751-5770-af18-c4d31a4dbca6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge 12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312526} {:answer/id #uuid "bdd90533-3806-5a8d-9c20-c624b5340f89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313463} {:answer/id #uuid "da8bac94-2af9-5d4f-bb9e-888341b229c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge -12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313690} {:answer/id #uuid "fe5260cf-2b88-59f4-aca6-f8fbf7c13e70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314004}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe5260cf-2b88-59f4-aca6-f8fbf7c13e70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314004} :answer-field/id #uuid "e23a6d1f-5fa6-5ea0-84c7-199794933e97" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314633}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e8a3cfa3-5dd8-5a89-8d0e-84651dbd2d63" :question/math-academy-id "q-341127" :question/problem "Use the Laplace transform of $f(t)={e}^{\\text{i}\\omega t}$ to find the Laplace transform of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12t).$$\\,L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12t)}=$ {{field-1}},\ndefined for {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The linearity property of the Laplace transform states that for functions $f(t)$ and $g(t),$ we have\n\n$$\nL{\\alpha f(t)+\\beta g(t)}=\\alpha \\cdot L{f(t)}+\\beta \\cdot L{g(t)},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants.\n\nFirst, recall that the sine function can be defined in terms of complex exponentials as follows: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12t)=\\frac{{e}^{12\\text{i}t}-{e}^{-12\\text{i}t}}{2\\text{i}}\n$$\n\nTaking the Laplace transform and applying the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12t)} & =L{\\frac{{e}^{12\\text{i}t}-{e}^{-12\\text{i}t}}{2\\text{i}}} \\\\  & =L{\\frac{{e}^{12\\text{i}t}}{2\\text{i}}-\\frac{{e}^{-12\\text{i}t}}{2\\text{i}}} \\\\  & =L{\\frac{{e}^{12\\text{i}t}}{2\\text{i}}}-L{\\frac{{e}^{-12\\text{i}t}}{2\\text{i}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\text{i}}L{{e}^{12\\text{i}t}}-\\frac{1}{2\\text{i}}L{{e}^{-12\\text{i}t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we recall that \n\n$$\nL{{e}^{\\text{i}\\omega t}}=\\frac{1}{s-\\text{i}\\omega },\\,s>0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{12\\text{i}t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-12\\text{i}},\\,s>0 \\\\ L{{e}^{-12\\text{i}t}} & =\\frac{1}{s+12\\text{i}},\\,s>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12t)} & =\\frac{1}{2\\text{i}}L{{e}^{12\\text{i}t}}-\\frac{1}{2\\text{i}}L{{e}^{-12\\text{i}t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s-12\\text{i}}-\\frac{1}{2\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s+12\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\text{i}}(\\frac{1}{s-12\\text{i}}-\\frac{1}{s+12\\text{i}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\text{i}}(\\frac{(s+12\\text{i})-(s-12\\text{i})}{(s-12\\text{i})(s+12\\text{i})}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\text{i}}(\\frac{24\\text{i}}{{s}^{2}+144}) \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{{s}^{2}+144},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ndefined for $s>0.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315054 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14436da6-7b8c-5459-99b4-6bfac4ea557e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5s}{{s}^{2}+25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312115} {:answer/id #uuid "1d9e4cdb-da70-58c7-89af-e8d816e8118a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{{s}^{2}-25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312197} {:answer/id #uuid "6a67d383-8250-5a1a-90d2-d860785ccd1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{{s}^{2}+25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312811} {:answer/id #uuid "e0a5bb4c-e052-588c-8333-00b1ec43ae2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313742} {:answer/id #uuid "f4191730-dc53-522b-bd9c-0a28f4609b05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313927}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0a5bb4c-e052-588c-8333-00b1ec43ae2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313742} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bd9d091-035d-5977-ba5e-edd708d5f7ff" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314383} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f877140-44e1-512e-aa01-58a47c03d18a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312212} {:answer/id #uuid "5787223e-84df-5b67-8318-493beb86482a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312680} {:answer/id #uuid "5d707f3b-b3d7-52ed-8c43-aff476c90d11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312722} {:answer/id #uuid "6f0cd83e-16f9-5e10-8198-cb4268d7ac22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312849} {:answer/id #uuid "c190ebbe-c34f-57a2-84bb-70203879f609" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge -5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313489} {:answer/id #uuid "d70e6448-340a-5c5d-bb7d-9a3c9421077e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313669}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5787223e-84df-5b67-8318-493beb86482a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312680} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7d45f06-6418-52b0-822f-68bc8cdb0326" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314460}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c15c9946-0f44-5115-b665-0c4efd18e05a" :question/math-academy-id "q-341137" :question/problem "Use the Laplace transform of $f(t)={e}^{\\text{i}\\omega t}$ to find the Laplace transform of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t).$$\\,L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)}=$ {{field-1}},\ndefined for {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The linearity property of the Laplace transform states that for functions $f(t)$ and $g(t),$ we have\n\n$$\nL{\\alpha f(t)+\\beta g(t)}=\\alpha \\cdot L{f(t)}+\\beta \\cdot L{g(t)},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants.\n\nFirst, recall that the cosine function can be defined in terms of complex exponentials as follows: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)=\\frac{{e}^{5\\text{i}t}+{e}^{-5\\text{i}t}}{2}\n$$\n\nTaking the Laplace transform and applying the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)} & =L{\\frac{{e}^{5\\text{i}t}+{e}^{-5\\text{i}t}}{2}} \\\\  & =L{\\frac{{e}^{5\\text{i}t}}{2}+\\frac{{e}^{-5\\text{i}t}}{2}} \\\\  & =L{\\frac{{e}^{5\\text{i}t}}{2}}+L{\\frac{{e}^{-5\\text{i}t}}{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{5\\text{i}t}}+\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{-5\\text{i}t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we recall that \n\n$$\nL{{e}^{\\text{i}\\omega t}}=\\frac{1}{s-\\text{i}\\omega },\\,s>0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{5\\text{i}t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-5\\text{i}},\\,s>0 \\\\ L{{e}^{-5\\text{i}t}} & =\\frac{1}{s+5\\text{i}},\\,s>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)} & =\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{5\\text{i}t}}+\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{-5\\text{i}t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s-5\\text{i}}+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s+5\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{s-5\\text{i}}+\\frac{1}{s+5\\text{i}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{(s+5\\text{i})+(s-5\\text{i})}{(s-5\\text{i})(s+5\\text{i})}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{2s}{{s}^{2}+25}) \\\\  & =\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+25},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ndefined for $s>0.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315056 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d0c4566c-bd79-5868-a603-18f0216abcb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{x}}{1+{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313607}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0c4566c-bd79-5868-a603-18f0216abcb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{x}}{1+{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313607} :answer-field/id #uuid "183d9fe6-f1f2-5fd2-b79e-60dbadd9be0a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314073}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c596781e-b79d-5304-abff-1db8b7bfbe7e" :question/math-academy-id "q-341146" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)={e}^{x}\\cdot arccot\\,x.$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)={e}^{x}\\,arccot\\,x\\,-$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $arccot$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccot\\,x)=-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x}\\cdot arccot\\,x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})\\cdot arccot\\,x+{e}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccot\\,x) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\,arccot\\,x+{e}^{x}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\,arccot\\,x-\\frac{{e}^{x}}{1+{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315057 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08831fa4-e925-511e-9c83-0ad4ccc9d162" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{log}_{4}x}{1+{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312036}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08831fa4-e925-511e-9c83-0ad4ccc9d162" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{log}_{4}x}{1+{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312036} :answer-field/id #uuid "b52cc14c-ea3a-52a9-8673-3631dde0a4af" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314499}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "88e0b1bd-ab5b-5056-934f-dc0524e7e997" :question/math-academy-id "q-341147" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)={log}_{4}⁡x\\cdot arccot\\,x.$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{arccot\\,x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\,-$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $arccot$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccot\\,x)=-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{4}⁡x\\cdot arccot\\,x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{4}⁡x)\\cdot arccot\\,x+{log}_{4}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccot\\,x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\cdot arccot\\,x+{log}_{4}⁡x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{arccot\\,x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-\\frac{{log}_{4}⁡x}{1+{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315060 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65d81e41-d413-5bdc-bac8-be87aebb35d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312778}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65d81e41-d413-5bdc-bac8-be87aebb35d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312778} :answer-field/id #uuid "283a6be5-839d-5ff0-9bb5-4cf7f3cc3f25" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314116} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "371c6c74-0468-5c9c-b71f-5ca91630b4ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312419}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "371c6c74-0468-5c9c-b71f-5ca91630b4ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312419} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c25f5fd-d7bd-5f84-a472-da9da0020049" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314435}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "61288950-c35e-5f57-a1be-6d007672017d" :question/math-academy-id "q-341179" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)=\\frac{{3}^{x}}{arccsc\\,x}.$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}} \n$\\frac{1}{arccsc\\,x}\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\frac{1}{|x|{(arccsc\\,x)}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we let $u(x)={3}^{x}$ and $v(x)=arccsc\\,x,$ and apply the quotient rule.\n\nWe use the formulae\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)={3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\text{and}\\,{v}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{({3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)\\cdot arccsc\\,x-{3}^{x}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}})}{{(arccsc\\,x)}^{2}}. \\\\  & ={3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot \\frac{arccsc\\,x}{{(arccsc\\,x)}^{2}}+\\frac{{3}^{x}}{{(arccsc\\,x)}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & ={3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\frac{1}{arccsc\\,x}+\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\frac{1}{|x|{(arccsc\\,x)}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315065 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46fdc275-923c-5cd3-a59b-4a658e3f4258" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{s}^{2}{F}^{″}(s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312553} {:answer/id #uuid "84e3b5f2-d37c-5878-a054-dc9361627378" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{s}^{2}{F}^{″}(s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313042} {:answer/id #uuid "aa724df4-aed9-56b9-b407-2a2e5a522b9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{F}^{″}(s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313312} {:answer/id #uuid "b4df4b8f-9398-5c59-ba04-dacf1a61413f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{F}^{″}(s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313383} {:answer/id #uuid "c3994cd8-7571-5ad3-a21b-c67bb4e8415b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{s}^{2}{F}^{′}(s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4df4b8f-9398-5c59-ba04-dacf1a61413f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{F}^{″}(s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313383} :answer-field/id #uuid "072ef1bc-6e04-55a4-b9ac-23763a27d11a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314031} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "170b0fa4-7eec-5f57-a0e3-d192a2d44d2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312137} {:answer/id #uuid "79a1e393-ba6c-57b2-83c4-d10fabbbf1c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}-16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312948} {:answer/id #uuid "c86b62b6-2702-55eb-8810-cdeedaaba6f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313540} {:answer/id #uuid "f554c7f1-c2db-5d22-a255-a910f3a71c68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313936}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "170b0fa4-7eec-5f57-a0e3-d192a2d44d2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312137} :answer-field/id #uuid "6aa5dcd4-7236-50c3-b140-eeeedbc4b4c6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314307} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20a21059-d54f-551e-9471-37938846fab3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{s}^{3}+96s}{({s}^{2}-16)^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312223} {:answer/id #uuid "6c979ee3-b3e6-5f6f-972c-b7c44c3eeccd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{s}^{2}+96}{({s}^{2}-16)^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312828} {:answer/id #uuid "a53b396b-e15e-5c11-8bf5-7819f11520ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2{s}^{2}+96}{({s}^{2}-16)^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313274} {:answer/id #uuid "b379d677-4668-58aa-91c7-83d7f21af605" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2{s}^{3}+96s}{({s}^{2}-16)^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313370}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20a21059-d54f-551e-9471-37938846fab3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{s}^{3}+96s}{({s}^{2}-16)^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312223} :answer-field/id #uuid "92b0b6b0-3213-508a-a594-6b878519058c" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314405} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ec5e059-a372-5ee6-a9ca-b72ae0e49495" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{s}^{3}+32s}{({s}^{2}-16)^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312346} {:answer/id #uuid "6a94e5f4-2a5c-576f-ada0-118b77c74565" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2{s}^{3}+96s}{({s}^{2}-16)^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312812} {:answer/id #uuid "ba16dbd1-da4e-5df4-8ce6-122d14f5c5d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2{s}^{3}+32s}{({s}^{2}-16)^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313425} {:answer/id #uuid "fe59aa68-ce10-51bf-a902-d1f9264f9d29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{s}^{3}+96s}{({s}^{2}-16)^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe59aa68-ce10-51bf-a902-d1f9264f9d29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{s}^{3}+96s}{({s}^{2}-16)^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314005} :answer-field/id #uuid "d28f2095-fdf6-5b95-93c2-162bb3d5a558" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314588}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7344131a-f847-5800-9b21-f09ea79674c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-341216" :question/problem "Suppose we wish to calculate the Laplace transform \n\n$$\nL{{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡4t}.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below. You may make use of the following result:\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡\\omega t}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-{\\omega }^{2}},\\,s>\\omega .\n$$\n\nLet $f(t)=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡4t$ and $F(s)=L{f(t)}.$ By the smoothness property of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{2}f(t)}={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe Laplace transform of $f(t)$ is\n\n$$\nF(s)=L{f(t)}={{field-2}},\\,s>4.\n$$\n\nWe have that\n\n$$\n{F}^{″}(s)={{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡4t}={{field-4}},\\,s>4.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If a function $f(t)$ is piecewise continuous on $[0,\\infty )$ and has exponential order $a,$ then its Laplace transform\n\n$$\nF(s)=L{f(t)}\n$$\n\nexists for every real $s>a,$ and $F$ is infinitely differentiable in this region of convergence. Moreover, for each integer $n\\ge 0$ and every such $s,$ we have\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{n}f(t)}=(-1)^{n}{F}^{(n)}(s).\n$$\n\nIn particular, for $n=2,$ we have\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{2}f(t)}={F}^{″}(s).\n$$\n\nWe have that $f(t)=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡4t.$ Using the given result with $\\omega =4,$ the Laplace transform of $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nF(s)=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-16},\\,s>4.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating with respect to $s,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-16}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(s({s}^{2}-16)^{-1}) \\\\  & =({s}^{2}-16)^{-1}+s(-({s}^{2}-16)^{-2}\\cdot 2s) \\\\  & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-16}{({s}^{2}-16)^{2}}-\\frac{2{s}^{2}}{({s}^{2}-16)^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{s}^{2}+16}{({s}^{2}-16)^{2}} \\\\ {F}^{″}(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\frac{{s}^{2}+16}{({s}^{2}-16)^{2}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{{s}^{2}+16}{({s}^{2}-16)^{2}}) \\\\  & =-(\\frac{({s}^{2}+16)^{′}\\cdot ({s}^{2}-16)^{2}-({s}^{2}+16)\\cdot {(({s}^{2}-16)^{2})}^{′}}{({s}^{2}-16)^{4}}) \\\\  & =-(\\frac{(2s)({s}^{2}-16)^{2}-({s}^{2}+16)\\cdot 2({s}^{2}-16)\\cdot 2s}{({s}^{2}-16)^{4}}) \\\\  & =-(\\frac{2s({s}^{2}-16)^{2}-4s({s}^{2}+16)({s}^{2}-16)}{({s}^{2}-16)^{4}}) \\\\  & =-(\\frac{2s({s}^{2}-16)-4s({s}^{2}+16)}{({s}^{2}-16)^{3}}) \\\\  & =-(\\frac{2{s}^{3}-32s-4{s}^{3}-64s}{({s}^{2}-16)^{3}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2{s}^{3}+96s}{({s}^{2}-16)^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we used the quotient rule to find ${F}^{″}(s).$\n\nTherefore, by the smoothness property,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡4t}={F}^{″}(s)=\\frac{2{s}^{3}+96s}{({s}^{2}-16)^{3}},\\,s>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315066 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26ff3440-ff04-5bfd-8fc1-687bd5f7d123" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{6}{{s}^{2}-36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312269} {:answer/id #uuid "3970154d-ce4b-5800-be35-0be84aafe76e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{{s}^{2}-36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312442} {:answer/id #uuid "7bafb52e-ec26-51b8-aad3-c2573738b82f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312965} {:answer/id #uuid "8bddb1f0-0b49-58eb-b758-5eeed60b541f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313094}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26ff3440-ff04-5bfd